,$ | $\\,¬P∨Q\\,$ | $\\,(P∧Q)∧(¬P∨Q)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-4}} |\n\nAccording to the table, $(P∧Q)∧(¬P∨Q)$ \n{{field-5}}\nalways false. Therefore, it \n{{field-6}} \na contradiction." :question/worked-solution "An expression is a contradiction if it is always false, regardless of the inputs.\n\nBy completing the final column in the truth table below, we obtain the following:\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,P∧Q\\,$ | $\\,¬P∨Q\\,$ | $\\,(P∧Q)∧(¬P∨Q)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nAccording to the table, $(P∧Q)∧(¬P∨Q)$ \n$\\text{isn't}$\nalways false. Therefore, it \n$\\text{isn't}$\na contradiction."} :step/id #uuid "e83a8f71-06ad-5f20-94e3-091c84463c75" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420437}}] :activity/title "Tautologies and Contradictions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420434}]}
